Dinacharya Launcher reads which apps you used and for how long, so it can show your phone time on the home screen and in your reports, and count the minutes for any daily app limit you set on the home screen.

It is read on this phone only. It is not sent to the developer or to anyone else. If you turn on Google Drive backup, your saved reports (including the names of the apps you used most) go to your own private space in your own Drive, and nowhere else.

Next, Android's settings open. Find Dinacharya Launcher in the list and switch it on. You can switch it off there at any time.{1}

